This is 99% Invisible. I'm Roman Mars. Two hours west of Duluth, there's a wide shallow lake called Big Rice Lake. Every summer, once the ice has thawed, the surface of the lake is slowly breached by tall green stalks that grow up and out of the water. By early fall, big rice lake is dotted with canoes full of people there to harvest the grains from those plants. This is where the lake gets its name. These tall, unassuming stems are full of a very special ingredient, wild rice. In my first time actually at at Rice and me and my sister took my grandma and my mother out on the lake and we were going around in circles and they were pointing. I want to go over there, I want to go over there.
这里是 99% Invisible，我是 Roman Mars。在德卢斯以西两小时车程的地方，有一个宽阔而浅的湖泊，叫大米湖（Big Rice Lake）。每年夏天，冰雪融化后，湖面上会慢慢长出高高的绿色茎秆，伸出水面。到了初秋，大米湖上点缀着载满人的独木舟，他们来这里收割这些植物的谷物。这就是湖名的由来。这些高大、不起眼的茎秆里装满了一种非常特殊的成分：野米。我第一次去大米湖时，我和姐姐带着奶奶和妈妈去湖上，我们绕着圈划船，她们指着说：“我想去那边，我想去那边。”

